title:: MIRa
summary:: Native spectral, pitch, onset, tonal, rhythm, auditory and wavelet analysis
categories:: Libraries>MIR
related:: Guides/MIRa-and-FluCoMa, Guides/MIRa-legacy-migration

MIRa provides 135 public classes for real-time musical analysis and analysis-driven sound. Each class page explains the technique, units, timing, limits and an audible example. Most return control-rate features; audio-input analyzers consume the full audio block internally. FFT readers preserve the shared buffer representation.

Pitch confidence, periodicity and voicing describe different evidence. Neither confidence nor tonal/rhythm labels imply calibrated recognition accuracy. Use matching FFT sizes and hops, allow analysis warmup, and increase server real-time memory for large filter banks or CQT kernels.

section:: Optional neural extension

The separately built MIRaNeural extension provides code::PitchPESTO::, a monophonic pitch estimator using PESTO v2's variable-Q frontend and learned convolutional network. It uses a native CPU implementation with an explicitly loaded, sample-rate-specific model buffer; no Python runtime or automatic download is involved. Its 10 ms update hop is distinct from its approximately 95–103 ms frame-center delay at 44.1/48/96 kHz. See its installed class help after adding MIRaNeural. Model export, supported configurations and current verification are documented in the extension README.

section:: Core

definitionlist::
## link::Classes/SpecCentroid2:: || Explicit spectral centroid in Hz.
