section:: Wavelets

Haar/db1 through db8 are supported. Periodic boundaries remain the default; the optional symmetric mode analyzes a reflected frame with redundant coefficients and preserves the same input-frame streaming delay.

definitionlist::
## link::Classes/Wavelets2:: || Daubechies scale energies, RMS or entropy contributions.
## link::Classes/WaveletBands:: || Multiscale wavelet energy bank.
## link::Classes/WaveletEntropy:: || Normalized entropy of wavelet scale energies.
## link::Classes/WaveletFlux:: || Positive change in normalized wavelet scale energies.
## link::Classes/WaveletCentroid:: || Energy-weighted center of wavelet scale frequencies.
## link::Classes/WaveletSpread:: || Spread around the wavelet scale-frequency center.
## link::Classes/WaveletDaub2:: || Daubechies analysis, coefficient removal and audio reconstruction.
::

section:: Examples and visualization

Class help files feature musically meaningful, individually designed sound processes and live MIR visualization GUIs via the code::MIRaGUI:: toolkit.

subsection:: Audio corpus
Examples load dedicated CC0 1.0 audio material bundled in the extension's code::sounds/:: folder via code::MIRaGUI.soundPath::, with graceful fallbacks to self-contained synthetic source graphs:
list::
## strong::drums.wav::: Acoustic drum groove with crisp transients, kick, snare, and hi-hats (ideal for onsets, rhythm, flux, and tempo).
## strong::piano-chords.wav::: Polyphonic grand piano progressions (ideal for chromagram, key, chord, and harmonic analysis).
## strong::melody.wav::: Sustained vocal and instrumental melody (ideal for monophonic pitch tracking, vibrato, and melodic contour).
## strong::plucks.wav::: Acoustic plucked acoustic strings (ideal for attack slope, decay time, and transient dynamics).
## strong::stereo.wav::: Dynamic acoustic stereo panorama with moving panning (ideal for stereo correlation, panning, and coherence).
## strong::bass-melody-mix.wav::: Multi-layer polyphonic mix (ideal for multipitch and predominant pitch extraction).
## strong::texture.wav::: Ambient sound texture evolving between harmonic tones and turbulent noise (ideal for entropy, flatness, and wavelet spread).
::
Each example can also take live microphone or line input by uncommenting the code::SoundIn.ar(0):: alternative.

subsection:: Live MIRaGUI visualizers
The extension provides 10 real-time GUI visualizers designed according to standard MIR practice:
list::
## strong::MIRaGUI.scope::: Real-time scrolling time-series oscilloscope with feature range bounds and engineering units.
## strong::MIRaGUI.bars::: Multi-band spectrum, filter bank, and cepstral bar monitor with peak hold decay and custom subband labels.
## strong::MIRaGUI.heatmap::: 2D scrolling waterfall spectrogram and tempogram display.
## strong::MIRaGUI.chroma::: 12-pitch-class circular polar radar wheel.
## strong::MIRaGUI.tonnetz::: 2D planar projection of 6-dimensional Tonnetz harmonic space (fifth, minor third, and major third axes).
## strong::MIRaGUI.stereo::: Polar goniometer (Lissajous X/Y phase scope) and stereo correlation meter.
## strong::MIRaGUI.pianoRoll::: Scrolling fundamental frequency tracker plotted on a musical MIDI note grid.
## strong::MIRaGUI.rhythm::: Circular tempo and beat phase dial.
## strong::MIRaGUI.tristimulus::: Barycentric ternary triangle displaying relative harmonic energy distribution (T1, T2, T3).
## strong::MIRaGUI.envelope::: Triggered transient envelope and attack/decay time-domain waveform scope.
::

section:: Verification and test suite

The test suite in code::tests/sc/:: verifies class library compilation, SCDoc help file syntax, and headless Non-Real-Time (NRT) audio rendering across all 135 UGens:
list::
## code::compile_check.scd::: Verifies clean class compilation.
## code::compile_help_examples.scd::: Parses and compiles all executable code blocks in every help file.
## code::verify_scdoc.scd::: Validates SCDoc indexing and document integrity.
## code::generate_example_check.py --nrt::: Automatically extracts and renders each UGen's help example via scsynth NRT, monitoring audio finite bounds, peak levels, and zero bad primitive calls.
::

section:: Further work

The native research extensions include ChromaCQT, multiband rhythm modulation, db1–db8 with symmetric boundaries, and extended chord templates. The neural audit selects PESTO v2 for a possible separate prototype; weight-license scope, frontend parity and real-time deployment remain unresolved. Recording-based accuracy and release qualification remain later work. See the installed docs/roadmap-status.md for exact evidence and limits.
